    "lawCode": "Amd §§240.00, Pen L",
    "lawSection": "Penal Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5512A\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the penal law, in relation to\nincluding community centers in the definition of \"public place\"\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nTo clarify that in connection with offenses against the public order,\na public place includes community centers.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 amends section 240.00 of the penal law to explicitly state\nthat in connection with offenses against the public order, a public\nplace includes community centers.\n\nSection 2 provides the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nSince the beginning of 2017, over 100 bomb threats have been called in\nto Jewish community centers across the country. These threats go hand\nin hand with a recent dramatic rise in anti-Semitic crime. These\nheinous acts are placing a strain upon communities and disrupting the\neveryday routine of affected centers, forcing unnecessary evacuations\nof adults, children and infants. More importantly, these threats\ncompromise the safety and well-being of those who work at and go to\nthese community centers.\n\nBy adding community centers to the definition of a public place, this\nlegislation clarifies that in connection with offenses against public\norder, a public place includes community centers. Placing a false bomb\nor hazardous material and falsely reporting an incident are both\noffenses against public order and both crimes reflect what is\nhappening in the case of threats to Jewish community centers.\n\nMaking this change to the public place definition will expressly allow\nfor those who perpetrate threats against community centers to be\ncharged with a public order offense.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect on the ninetieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law.\n",
